From b962bfe8dc0b520640741ffac037cfbb0b82bb8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:27:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] arm: zte: add support for ZTE Sanechips ZX279125 and VSOL
 V2801SG

Add board and SoC support for ZTE Sanechips ZX279125 ARMv7 Cortex-A9 SoC
and the VSOL V2801SG GPON ONT board.

Features included in this port:
- Device tree zx279125-vsol-v2801sg.dts (16 MiB DRAM below PPE buffer pool)
- Native ZX279125 hardware timer driver (12.5 MHz)
- Native ZX279125 UART driver (25 MHz, 115200 8N1)
- Early debug UART support
- Native SPI flash controller driver (SPIFC) with ZB25VQ64 NOR support
- Persistent SPI flash environment located at 0x7a0000 (usercfg partition)
- Native Gigabit Ethernet driver (zx279125_eth):
  - Hardware DMA with 16 dedicated 32-bit queue registers
  - Standalone cold-start hardware initialization (BMU, BPT, Rings)
  - Dynamic runtime cursor table validation and adoption
  - Memory write/read barriers for cache and DMA coherency
- Board reset controller support

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
